> Explain why deterministic validation matters when optimizing a GPU inference kernel.
# Why Deterministic Validation Matters for GPU Inference Kernels

When optimizing GPU kernels, you're making trade-offs that can subtly change numerical results. Deterministic validation is the safety net that lets you trust those optimizations. Here's why it matters:

## 1. Distinguishing Bugs from Expected Numerical Variation

GPU optimizations often reorder floating-point operations (via different loop unrolling, reduction orders, or fused operations). Since floating-point addition isn't associative, these reordering changes produce *slightly different* results.

